# Boarding passes of a return trip, one per page, on a custom page size of 210 × 99 mm (Width and Height in Page).
# Each pass is a card with rounded corners over a grey sheet: a Grid of two columns, the pass and the stub, split by
# a dashed line (Border style: dashed) with two notches cut at its ends (Page overlay circles of the colour of the
# sheet). The airports and the flight time share a baseline (Vertical: baseline in a Stack) although their sizes
# differ, the details go in a Grid of labels and values, the pass carries the PDF417 barcode that gate readers scan
# (Barcode format: pdf417, with the data of the IATA boarding pass) and the stub, a Code 128 of the booking
# reference with its readable text. The airline mark is a small SVG.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Width: 210mm
		Height: 99mm
		Margin: 6mm
	Title: Boarding passes · Ingrid Halvorsen · Lisbon and Oslo
	Subject: Boarding passes of booking EK7Q2M, flights NW418 and NW419
	Author: Northwind Air
	Language: en
	Page overlay:
		Id: sheet
		Offset: -6mm
		Layer: -2
		Box:
			Background: #DCE4E8
	Page overlay:
		Id: notch-top
		Offset: -3mm auto auto 135mm
		Block:
			Style: notch
	Page overlay:
		Id: notch-bottom
		Offset: auto auto -3mm 135mm
		Block:
			Style: notch
	Section:
		Id: outbound
		Grid:
			Id: pass-outbound
			Style: pass
			Area:
				Block:
					Style: main
					Stack:
						Style: band
